{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style","id":1405298,"title":"I don't get Falcon Style","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-30T04:16:11-07:00","id":1405298,"title":"I don't get Falcon Style","content":"What it says on the tin.<br /> Falcon is this weird mix of wanting you to attack from above, but it's first signature move, Raptor's Fatal Descent, leaves you prone, which prevents you from getting airborne again easily.<br /> A lot of it's bennies support grapples, but it kind of wants you to fly/jump up and swoop down again and it's not super great at dragging someone with you, so it apparently wants you to throw people a lot, I guess?<br /> <br /> Falcon also has a whopping 4 Simple Charms, which are incompatible with each other, well, because they're Simple type charms. I just don't get it.<br /> What's the synergy? It just seems like a bunch of random unconnected Charms that do neat things, but how is it a style?<br /> <br /> Since Centipede, Swaying Grass Dance, and Laughing Monster, all also from Lunars, make instant sense to me, I refuse to believe it's a badly written style. In fact, Lunars is an incredibly well-written book, so I assume I'm just not processing something right?<br /> <br /> Can anyone give me a short rundown on why, from a mechanics perspective, I would want to use Falcon? I am already sold on it's fluff, that is a very stylish... Style. But even if I were a winged Lunar wanting to throw people from up high, I'd probably be better off just using Mantis.<br /> <br /> What am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:13:19-07:00","id":1405339,"title":"","content":"Falcon Style very wants you to come on and slam, yes, which Grasping Raptor Clutch lets you do reflexively after jumping to vertical short range with someone. Assuming your fall back down from that jump isn\u2019t supposed to happen until your next turn (which just feels correct to me in general and this style is direct evidence for because its best shenanigans don\u2019t work otherwise), it\u2019s Raptor\u2019s Fatal Descent time. Then Flacon Takes Flight triviliazes a rise from prone/disengage flurry so you\u2019re ready in one turn for your next ground pound.<br /> <br /> Raking Talon Kick is clearly meant to follow Hare-Killing Death Dive or Neck-Piercing Hook and can explicitly be combined with Raptor\u2019s Fatal Descent so it really doesn\u2019t matter that they\u2019re all Simple.<br /> <br /> And then you pretty much switch back and forth between those tactics as you feel like until it\u2019s time to wow the crowd with <s>Lightning Strikes Twice</s> Doom Plummets Down.<br /> <br /> Welcome to the Space Jam, here\u2019s your mask. That Immaculate who thinks she can defeat El Toro is the ball.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13313,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","user":"Sith_Happens","date":". 07-30-2020, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:20:11-07:00","id":1405341,"title":"","content":"Let's see...<br /> <br /> First a look into the Simples:<br /> <br /> a Simple for &quot;dive-in decisive for adding up to 5 hit threshold to damage (may sometimes make a second move!). You are also prone but don't care too much about it&quot;<br /> a Simple for &quot;grapple++ that prones without a throw and steals init (usually enough to make up for the gambit cost)&quot;<br /> a Simple for &quot;far-throw with a secondary damage proc&quot;<br /> a Simple for &quot;post-throw decisive that adds foregone control to damage again. you may combo this with the first simple for a total of foregone control + hit threshold extra damage&quot;<br /> The capstone is a post-throw extra decisive attack, with extra damage and may be used after a decisive for nearly as much damage as the previous one.<br /> <br /> From these the presumption is that you want to force an engage-&gt;grapple-&gt;throw loop. If you can't grapple, disengage to reengage.<br /> You also have access to Smashing weapons, which on its own allows this dynamic with non-grapple attacks (withering, especially) in exchange for losing a bit of init and defense, and not doing the grapple's comparatively high damages.<br /> So long as you can meet either expectation your throws and decisives are on steroids.<br /> <br /> <br /> The style doesn't have withering damage adders, in practice, but gives you an extremely reliable attack booster provided you are forcing your preferred engagement modes (2m to nearly double your hit chances against the 4-9 defense range, and your excellency will outpace a straight defense adder) and powerful Control rolls.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> On your Enablers to play on that loop:<br /> <br /> You need a good engaging and a good disengaging tool. That's Falcon Takes Flight. FTF also trivializes Rising From Prone for when you use Fatal Descent.<br /> You also benefit from ways to easily reposition enemies without losing damage. That's Grasping Raptor Clutch and Smashing Weapons.<br /> <br /> You need elevation to get some of those bonuses and attacks. That's your Form.with its free monkey leaps. The form also gives you a boost to control rolls.<br /> <br /> Form + grasping raptor clutch also gives you a 1-round combo of &quot;throw hard and force a short range fall damage&quot; that only relies on beating the enemy's control roll by 2.<br /> <br /> Proning keeps you alive:<br /> Against a prone enemy, your attacks are easier to hit (-1/-2 defense) and their attacks are harder to land (-3 to attack). If the enemy tries to rise from prone he's still going to be hampered on attack because of the flurry...or give up attacking entirely(armor adds a penalty here, flurrying can be very very expensive). If the enemy is grappled he can't even do that (another -1 to -3 to attack, and can't rise until released)<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Summing up:<br /> <br /> I expect the accomplished Falcon fighter will start with with either:<br /> 1) engage + grapple to get an immediate big savage (either withering or decisive) and proning and maybe get the form up<br /> 2) attack + disengage, go back to 1 and most likely get the form up (and after the form is up this disengage will always succeed, no roll necessary).<br /> <br /> Followed by a huge throw (withering or decisive, potentially dealing a good 50% more damage than normal) or some ground &amp; pound if the grapple is broken.<br /> <br /> From the throw you can immediately follow up with a boosted decisive, and disengage/smash to restart. (Raking Talon Kick will frequently stack +5 to +10 damage here, so even at base initiative you can reliably aggravate wound penalties)<br /> From the ground &amp; pound you may disengage or smash and restart.<br /> <br /> Doom Plummets Down not only gives you an extra attack (essentially doubling your decisive / making a withering-decisive in a single round), it also lets you double up on Raking Talon Kick, essentially tripling the gained damage from giving up control rounds on a throw: once on the throw, once on DPD and again on RTK (+Fatal Descent for good measure).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Against an enemy they can't grapple the focus shifts to the stylist moving in and out of range all the time, preferably up, to exploit the reliable attack booster and Fatal Descent..<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> They are partially countered by fighters that can casually fight prone (tiger, swaying grass iirc?) or reflexively rise from prone.<br /> They are partially countered by not wanting to savage (the def penalty from grappling and the loss of control is a big risk against multiple enemies, so you want to throw immediately)<br /> They are almost completely countered by enemies they can't grapple or smash.<br /> <br /> <br /> Solars and Sids are much bouncier (fear the sid whose attack dice only fail on a 3), while lunars can grapple most enemies that would break this style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 07-30-2020, 12:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T08:42:40-07:00","id":1405348,"title":"","content":"It seems fairly straightforward to me. Raptor\u2019s Fatal Descent is a finishing move that costs a willpower, I don\u2019t think you\u2019re supposed to use it more than once per fight. Everything else seems to be about landing grapples, and then either making your target prone, or dragging them away upwards to slam them down a whole range band plus decisive damage plus control rounds. Being both grappled and prone gives your target a -4 penalty to Evasion and -3 to Parry, as well as a -4 penalty to attacks, or -6 if they\u2019re using a two handed weapon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-30T10:09:06-07:00","id":1405376,"title":"","content":"Falcon Style is very good if you're a mobility focused character or a luchador. Falcon Takes Flight has good synergy with wings or Monkey Leap Technique, and if you have a way to stay in the air, you can use it to repeatedly set up Swift Talon Strike and Raptor's Fatal Descent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24948-hamsandlich","name":"HamSandLich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24948_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T01:40:33-07:00","id":1405759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405341#post1405341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's Falcon Takes Flight. FTF also trivializes Rising From Prone for when you use Fatal Descent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it though?<br /> Because you can't take movement actions other than Rise from Prone while you're prone, so you wouldn't be able to use FTF unless I'm overlooking something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T06:03:57-07:00","id":1405784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HamSandLich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405376#post1405376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Falcon Style is very good if you're a mobility focused character<b> or a luchador</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Next character confirmed","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T07:53:41-07:00","id":1405790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405759#post1405759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does it though?<br /> Because you can't take movement actions other than Rise from Prone while you're prone, so you wouldn't be able to use FTF unless I'm overlooking something?</div> </div> </div> </div>FTF enhances Rise From Prone. By MA 3 it clears the difficulty entirely on its own.<br /> On rounds you fall prone you will usually deploy FTF once or twice: One to rise from prone if you are concerned with your roll, and again to disengage after that. <br /> <br /> And if you still want to attack the enemy you just have to flurry (rise from prone + attack). If the attack connects using FTF to move away is guaranteed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2020, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T12:28:34-07:00","id":1405825,"title":"","content":"But doesn't my rise from prone use up my movement action? So I attack, and FTF gives me a reflexive movement action I can't use because I'm prone, and rising from prone isn't a movement action...<br /> <br /> Though I just realize you can just get Cat-Footed Grace to fix that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T16:01:28-07:00","id":1405848,"title":"","content":"Rise from Prone is a combat action. You can flurry to Rise and Attack, and still have your movement left.<br /> <br /> (i think. it's also under movement actions, gotta think on it a bit)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 08-01-2020, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-01T17:23:34-07:00","id":1405855,"title":"","content":"I think it is a movement action, but also how often are you spamming Raptor\u2019s Fatal Descent and it\u2019s not the final attack in the combat? If you didn\u2019t buff your willpower you get six uses of it over two days, assuming you never use Doom Plummets Down, resist social influence, spend it for an autosuccesses or anything else. <br /> <br /> You can use FTF to auto-rise from prone the turn after if you want though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T00:30:35-07:00","id":1405891,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah sure, I mean it's not a huge no-no, I'm just trying to fully understand the mechanics. And as I see it you would use RFD, which resets you to base and prones you, so your victim, if it's not crashed, has a good chance of going first next round, before you get to rise from prone. And it also means, without Cat-Footed Grace you're not using FTF.<br /> I mean sure, you can smash your opponent with RFD, so you're both prone, at least.<br /> By now I'm getting a grasp on Falcon, so TY all you guys. <br /> Just stumbled over the idea of &quot;FTF trivializes Rise From Prone&quot;, because it doesn't, it's still using a combat action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T00:41:56-07:00","id":1405894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405848#post1405848\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rise from Prone is a combat action. You can flurry to Rise and Attack, and still have your movement left.<br /> <br /> (i think. it's also under movement actions, gotta think on it a bit)</div> </div> </div> </div>By my read, no. One movement action per turn, with the noted exception that you can Rush in the same turn you Move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1424-ghanjrho","name":"GhanjRho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1424_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:13:01-07:00","id":1405906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405891#post1405891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah sure, I mean it's not a huge no-no, I'm just trying to fully understand the mechanics. And as I see it you would use RFD, which resets you to base and prones you, so your victim, if it's not crashed, has a good chance of going first next round, before you get to rise from prone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Fatal Decent lets you ignore the penalties of being prone. You are running your full numbers there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T03:52:34-07:00","id":1405911,"title":"","content":"Oh I did forget, well, that's a nice benny, at least.<br /> I guess it's just that it's all a very neat toolbox without the obvious combos some other styles boast. I remain thankful for all you guys time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:03:07-07:00","id":1405921,"title":"","content":"This is all you need to know about the style. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/d2/e9/13/d2e913a60ad4716378494b9cd093fc9e.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T06:53:44-07:00","id":1405936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405911#post1405911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I did forget, well, that's a nice benny, at least.<br /> I guess it's just that it's all a very neat toolbox without the obvious combos some other styles boast. I remain thankful for all you guys time!</div> </div> </div> </div>For Lunars if you are Legendary Sized and they aren't and/or a Solar, it's pretty decent for no-contest direct damage. (Though some argument can be made that the Lunar native charmset has more than enough grapple goodness).<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.tenor.com/images/d85d9f198d6b18d52267ef60314e7220/tenor.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T15:32:23-07:00","id":1406010,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1325840-effectively-using-soaring-zephyr-flight\">I wrote a thread</a> about how Dragon-Blooded could most effectively employ their &quot;flying&quot; Charm, Soaring Zephyr Flight, which has a number of restrictions.<br /> <br /> One post focused on how that Charm would work with Falcon Style.<br /> <br /> I'd forgotten what pissed me off about Falcon Style, but digging in has reminded me.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Neck-Piercing Hook&quot; completely fails to account for what happens when you throw an enemy when you're standing at least one range band above the ground.</b><br /> <br /> For a Style that explicitly enables you to grapple an opponent and carry him upwards with you before slamming him back down to the earth below, this is outrageous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:04:22-07:00","id":1406016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cheshire Cat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1405891#post1405891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just stumbled over the idea of &quot;FTF trivializes Rise From Prone&quot;, because it doesn't, it's still using a combat action.</div> </div> </div> </div>A combat action that you can flurry with a disengage action that can also get +3 successes with FTF.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T17:24:32-07:00","id":1406020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1406016#post1406016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combat action that you can flurry with a disengage action that can also get +3 successes with FTF.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice catch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T13:19:23-07:00","id":1406139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1406016#post1406016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A combat action that you can flurry with a disengage action that can also get +3 successes with FTF.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh right! So that's how that works!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T14:34:32-07:00","id":1406150,"title":"","content":"Wait a minute.<br /> <br /> You can only take one movement action per turn, which includes the reflexive Move action. The Rush action explicitly doesn't count against the limit, at least in regards to taking a reflexive Move action.<br /> <br /> Can you really Rise From Prone AND Disengage in the same turn, even with a flurry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T01:48:12-07:00","id":1406234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1406010#post1406010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Neck-Piercing Hook&quot; completely fails to account for what happens when you throw an enemy when you're standing at least one range band above the ground.</b><br /> <br /> For a Style that explicitly enables you to grapple an opponent and carry him upwards with you before slamming him back down to the earth below, this is outrageous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems pretty obvious to me - they take falling damage, then they take throw damage. Or maybe the other way around. It probably doesn't matter.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T07:14:47-07:00","id":1406267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>aluminiumtrioxid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1405298-i-don-t-get-falcon-style?p=1406234#post1406234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It seems pretty obvious to me - they take falling damage, then they take throw damage. Or maybe the other way around. It probably doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems legit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}